.SS " Tuple[str, int, Dict[str, Any]] pip\&._vendor\&.rich\&.console\&.Console\&._caller_frame_info (int offset, Callable[[], Optional[FrameType]]  currentframe = \fCinspect\&.currentframe\fP)\fC [static]\fP, \fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Get caller frame information\&.

Args:
    offset (int): the caller offset within the current frame stack\&.
    currentframe (Callable[[], Optional[FrameType]], optional): the callable to use to
        retrieve the current frame\&. Defaults to ``inspect\&.currentframe``\&.

Returns:
    Tuple[str, int, Dict[str, Any]]: A tuple containing the filename, the line number and
        the dictionary of local variables associated with the caller frame\&.

Raises:
    RuntimeError: If the stack offset is invalid\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " None pip\&._vendor\&.rich\&.console\&.Console\&._check_buffer ( self)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Check if the buffer may be rendered\&. Render it if it can (e\&.g\&. Console\&.quiet is False)
Rendering is supported on Windows, Unix and Jupyter environments\&. For
legacy Windows consoles, the win32 API is called directly\&.
This method will also record what it renders if recording is enabled via Console\&.record\&.

.fi
.PP
 
